  "texts": {
    "preamble": "M/S.Lakshmi Traders vs The Designated Officer (Thanjavur ... on 21 November, 2024 Author: M.S.Ramesh Bench: M.S.Ramesh W.A.(MD).No. Before The Madurai Bench Of Madras High Court Dated: 21.11.2024 Coram The Honourable Mr.Justice M.S.Ramesh And The Honourable Dr.Justice A.D.Maria Clete W.A.(MD).No.2393 of 2024 M/s.Lakshmi Traders, Represented by its Managing Partner, S.Selvakumar. ... Appellant/Petitioner Vs. 1.The Designated Officer (Thanjavur District), Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Office of the Deputy Director of Health Services, Gandhi Road, Thanjavur - 613 001. 2.Food Safety Officer, (Thirupanandhal Block and Thiruvidaimarudur Block), Fso Code 217, Tamil Nadu Food Safety and Drug Administration, Office of the Deputy Director of Health Services, Gandhi Road, Thanjavur - 613 001. 3.The Inspector of Police, Thiruvidaimaruthur Police Station, Thiruvidaimaruthur, Thanjavur District. (Fir in Crime No.985/2022) ... Respondents/Respon Page 1 of 5 M/S.Lakshmi Traders vs The Designated Officer (Thanjavur ... on 21 November, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/8779925/ 1 https://www.mhc.tn.gov.in/judis W.A.(Md). Prayer: Writ Appeal filed under Clause 15 of Letters Patent, praying to aside the impugned order passed in W.P.(MD).No.8968 of 2023 dated 05.06.2023 passed by this Court and allow this Writ Appeal. For Appellant : Mr.P.M.Vishnuvarthanan For R-1 & R-2 : Mr.S.Shaji Bino Additional Government Pleader For R-3 : Mr.P.Kottai Chamy Government Advocate (Crl. Side) Judgment",
    "facts": "The present Writ Appeal has been filed challenging the order passed by the learned Single Judge in W.P.(MD).No.8968 of 2023 dated 05.06.2023. 2. Thoug h other grounds have been raised by the appellant herein challenging the order passed in the Writ Petition in W.P.(MD).No.8968 of 2023 dated 05.06.2023",
    "arguments": ", the learned counsel for the appellant would submit that he is not pressing any of the grounds and that the appellant had preferred an appeal before the first respondent under Section 46(4) of the Food Safety and Standards Act, 2006 against the report of the Food Analysis Laboratory dated 23.11.2022, which may be directed to be disposed of within a time frame."
  },
